#, fuzzy
msgctxt "TC_HELP_RADIO_TWO_SERIAL_FORMAT"
msgid "The serial frame for the CAT port as data bits, parity and stop bits in the compact terminal-program notation: 8N2 means 8 data bits, no parity, 2 stop bits. Data bits may be 7 or 8, parity N (none), O (odd) or E (even), stop bits 1 or 2. When this command is not set, TR4W uses the radio's own documented defaults, so most operators never need it; set it only when your rig is configured for a non-standard frame. The baud rate is separate (RADIO TWO BAUD RATE). Also settable from the radio dialog's DATA/PARITY/STOP drop-down."
